{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>וְכַנָּה</b> — these are Israel, and the witness: אָמַצְתָּ לְּךָ." "Further: <b>אֲשֶׁר נָטַעָה יְמִינְךָ</b> — like וְתִטְּעֶהָ, and the word וּפְקֹד draws another after it, even though it is in a different verse, like: כִּי אָמַר גֵּר הָיִיתִי, with כִּי אֱלֹהֵי אָבִי בְּעֶזְרִי, and so it is: וּפְקֹד כַּנָּה." "<b>כַּנָּה</b> — an epithet for the vine or for the vine-stock that is established (מְכוֹנָנֶת). And some say: that the kaf is in place of gimel, but we have not found that they interchange except shin with samekh and the letters alef, heh, vav, yod." "And some say: that בְּכַנָּה — it should have been כִּנָּה, on the pattern of: רַבָּה צְבָאֲךָ. And R. Judah Halevi, may his memory be blessed, said: that the nun lacks a dagesh of the joining of two nuns, like הַלְלוּהוּ, from the heavy binyan with dagesh, imperative form. And thus he said, and likewise ben Naḥum, may his memory be blessed, in his opinion [or: in my opinion], the corrector [?]. And regarding the word עַל as imperative, like: אֵל נָא צַו אֶת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, opposite יְכַרְסְמֶנָּה." "And the word <b>בֵּן</b> — branch, like: בֵּן פֹּרָת יוֹסֵף."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 80, :notes {1 "The syntactic logic of the parallelism between verses is compressed and elliptical; rendered literally.", 3 "The attribution chain after R. Judah Halevi is textually compressed and possibly corrupt; the phrases בן נ״ל and אנ״י יא״י could not be resolved with confidence. 'The corrector' (המגי״ה) is read as referring to a masoretic or textual corrector."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:46.928880047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}